---
import Container from "../components/Container.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import SectionHeader from "../components/SectionHeader.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout title="Privacy — Conclave AX" description="How Conclave AX approaches privacy for people, Workspaces, Workers, and Accounts.">
  <Section>
    <Container>
      <SectionHeader eyebrow="Privacy" title="Privacy is part of the architecture." description="Conclave AX is architected with strict boundary separation to protect user credentials, source repositories, and execution telemetry." headingLevel={1} />
      <div class="legal-content">
        <h2>Human identity and Workspace data</h2>
        <p>Conclave Cloud uses human authentication (such as WebAuthn passkeys) to verify identity, then strictly scopes access based on Workspace membership and project permissions. Workspace chats, runs, and artifacts remain confidential to authorized members.</p>

        <h2>Accounts and external AI providers</h2>
        <p>Accounts represent external AI identities (e.g. OpenAI or Anthropic credentials). They are private by default. When shared within a Workspace, Conclave AX enables authorized execution without exposing plaintext secrets. Usage remains attributable to the requester and Account owner.</p>

        <h2>Workspaces and Workers</h2>
        <p>Workspaces are distinct execution identities. Workers execute in supervised processes behind a Workspace daemon and do not receive ambient machine permissions or Conclave Cloud master keys. Source files and build artifacts remain on your Workspace machine unless explicitly exported.</p>

        <h2>Telemetry and Public Website</h2>
        <p>This public website uses minimal, privacy-first, same-origin telemetry without cross-site tracking cookies. No credentials, source code, or private Workspace data are collected through this public site.</p>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>
</SiteLayout>
